<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4929] onePhase tx for invoke may fail on changing topology</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4929</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;One phase tx for invoke may fail in this scenario:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;backup did not rebalanced partition yet&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;in this case primary sends on backup new value instead of entry processor, in this case on backup we loose information about value calculated by entry processor&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;primary fails before it receives response from backup, client sends &apos;check&apos; request on backup to get return value, but return value on backup does not contain expected invoke result&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Added test IgniteOnePhaseCommitInvokeTest.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
